    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Prime Development Site – Bohernasup, Ballina, Co. Mayo\r\n\r\nFor Sale: c. 3.6 hectares (8.92 acres) of prime development land\r\n\r\nA substantial and strategically located parcel of development land extending to approximately 3.6 hectares (8.92 acres) is offered for sale in Bohernasup, Ballina, Co. Mayo.\r\n\r\nThe lands are zoned Strategic Residential Reserve under the Ballina Development Plan 2024–2030, presenting an attractive long-term development and investment opportunity. Maps in advert are for illustration purposes only.\r\n\r\nOccupying a high-profile position within one of Ballina's established and sought-after residential areas, the site is ideally situated close to a wide range of amenities and recreational facilities. Nearby landmarks include Ballina Football Club, Ballina Athletic Club, Ballina Beverages (Coca-Cola), Belleek Woods and the River Moy. The property is also surrounded by a number of established, highly regarded residential developments.\r\n\r\nThe site benefits from excellent accessibility, with access available from both Bohernasup Road and French Road, further enhancing its development potential.\r\n\r\nLocation\r\nBallina is the second-largest town in County Mayo and has a population of approximately 10,556 (Census 2022). The town is an important commercial and retail centre for the region and attracts visitors from a wide surrounding area. Renowned as the Salmon Capital of Ireland and located on the Wild Atlantic Way, Ballina offers a strong combination of amenities, employment, tourism and recreational facilities.\r\n\r\nThe town benefits from excellent public transport connections, including rail and bus services, while Ireland West Airport Knock is approximately 41km away.\r\n\r\nApproximate distances include:\r\n\r\nSligo: 60km\r\n\r\nGalway City: 113km\r\n\r\nDublin: 237km\r\n\r\nIreland West Airport Knock: 41km\r\n\r\nThe Opportunity\r\nThis is a significant landholding in an established residential location, offering an exceptional opportunity for developers, investors or those seeking a substantial strategic land investment in Ballina.\r\n\r\nKey features:\r\n\r\nc. 3.6 hectares (8.92 acres)\r\n\r\nStrategic Residential Reserve zoning\r\n\r\nLocated within an established and sought-after residential area\r\n\r\nAccess from Bohernasup Road and French Road\r\n\r\nClose to schools, sports facilities, retail and recreational amenities\r\n\r\nAdjacent to established residential developments\r\n\r\nExcellent accessibility and connectivity\r\n\r\nClose to Belleek Woods and the River Moy\r\n\r\nStrong strategic location within Ballina town\r\n\r\nFurther information and particulars are available from the selling agent.\r\n\r\nInterested parties are advised to satisfy themselves regarding all planning, zoning, servicing, access and development matters with the relevant authorities"
      }
    ],
